      "direction": "Directions for questions 1 to 25: Select the correct alternative from the given choices.",
      "text": "Consider a system with four processes A, B, C and D and ‘m’ instances of resource ‘r’. The resource requirements are 5, 7, 3 and 4 instances of resource ‘r’ respectively. What is the minimum value of ‘m’, hence system is dead lock free?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "7"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "16"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "19"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "15"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "16",
      "explanation": "Method 1: Each process requirement is Sᵢ for process ‘i’.\nSᵢ – A, B, C, D = 5, 7, 3, 4.\nAssume for each process i, (Sᵢ – 1) resources are allocated: 4, 6, 2, 3.\nThis system state result in deadlock i.e., the system with ≤15 resources may lead to deadlock. If atleast one extra resource available in this state, the system becomes deadlock free. ∴ 16 resources required.\nMethod 2:\n∑ Sᵢ < (m + n)\nSᵢ – resources required for process ‘i’.\nm – number of resources in system\nn – number of process in system.\n(5 + 7 + 3 + 4) < m + 4 ⇒ m = 16\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
